{
  "_id": "hevc-pipeline",
  "name": "HEVC Pipeline",
  "description": "HEVC-target transcode + audio/track cleanup pipeline. Every file: validate-before (health check), DV gate (P5/P7 hold, P8 continue), DEE audio (lossless English -> DD+/Atmos-aware, native ffmpeg E-AC3 fallback), keep English+untagged audio (drop non-English, commentary, descriptive), drop non-English subs / cover-art / data streams, remux to MKV, validate-after (duration ratio), pass -> /data/media (in place), fail -> /data/quarantine + review. Video handling by codec: already-HEVC sources are REMUXED ONLY (audio stripped, video copied, no re-encode); non-HEVC (incl. AV1) is hardware-encoded to HEVC via hardwareType=auto -- hevc_qsv on the A380 node, libx265 CPU fallback (CQ 24 <=1440p, CQ 27 4K+; preset slow), 10-bit Main10 preserved. checkOverallBitrate still spares low-bitrate NON-HEVC sources from a pointless encode (they remux like HEVC). The compareFileSize growth guard was REMOVED 2026-08-29 (the working file always replaces the original). The former already-HEVC short-circuit was removed the same day so HEVC files also get audio-stripped. Managed by scripts/configure_tdarr.py -- edit THIS file in git, never the Tdarr UI copy.",
